    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nHi,\n\nwith\n> feat(runtime): replace netrw with a very small script #39723\n\nthe netrw replacement leaves a lot of navigation buffers (directories) open.\nI think it would be nice, if every previous navigation buffer gets automatically closed, when a file is opened from that script.\n\n\n```bash\ncd ~\nnvim --clean ~\n```\n\n```vim\n\" navigate to a file\n\" open that file\n\" check open buffers\n:buffers\n  1  h-  \"~\"                            line 2\n  2  h-  \"~/.config\"                    line 26\n  3  h-  \"~/.config/nvim\"               line 5\n  4  h-  \"~/.config/nvim/lua\"           line 1\n  5 #h-  \"~/.config/nvim/lua/personal\"  line 3\n  6 %a   \"~/.config/nvim/lua/personal/lsp.lua\" line 1\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nno \"directory\" buffer should be left, it a file was opend via this script",
    "closed_at": "2026-06-27T18:08:30Z",
    "closed_by": {
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4",
