            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> the netrw replacement leaves a lot of navigation buffers (directories) open.\n\nI think this is the correct default behavior since it treats directory buffers the same as any other file buffer (although I believe it doesn't respect `'hidden'`, we should probably fix that). However, I can definitely see the use of closing directory buffers when a new directory is opened from that directory and the buffer does not exist in any other windows... so that should probably be configurable somehow.",
